},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MXLLineDetail"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxllinedetail\/init(line:width:color:linekind:printsobject:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLineDetail"]]},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLLineDetail":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLLineDetail","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLLineDetail","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"If the staff-lines element is present, the appearance of each line may be individually specified with a line-"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"detail type. Staff lines are numbered from bottom to top. The print-object attribute allows lines to be hidden"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"within a staff. This is used in special situations such as a widely-spaced percussion staff where a note"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"placed below the higher line is distinct from a note placed above the lower line. Hidden staff lines are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"included when specifying clef lines and determining display-step \/ display-octave values, but are not counted"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as lines for the purposes of the system-layout and staff-layout elements."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLineDetail","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxllinedetail","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLLineDetail","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLColor":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The color type indicates the color of an element. Color may be represented as hexadecimal RGB triples, as in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"HTML, or as hexadecimal ARGB tuples, with the A indicating alpha of transparency. An alpha value of 00 is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"totally transparent; FF is totally opaque. If RGB is used, the A value is assumed to be FF."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlcolor","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLColor","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLLineKind":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLLineKind","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLineKind","abstract":[{"text":"The line-type type distinguishes between solid, dashed, dotted, and wavy lines.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLLineKind"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLLineKind"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxllinekind"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLLineDetail/init(line:width:color:lineKind:printsObject:)":{"role":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLineDetail\/init(line:width:color:lineKind:printsObject:)","title":"init(line:width:color:lineKind:printsObject:)","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"line"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLStaffLineV","text":"MXLStaffLine"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"width"},{"kind":"